auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{pat}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // Act inside the Cluster IAM organization. Request 01 looks the org up by name and stores `orgId`;
  // admin API calls (instance level) are sent without the header so a stale `orgId` can't break them.
  const orgId = bru.getEnvVar("orgId");
  if (orgId && !req.getUrl().includes("/admin/v1/")) {
    req.setHeader("x-zitadel-orgid", orgId);
  }
}

docs {
  # Zitadel setup for a new hello-azure cluster

  Automates sections 3 and 3.x of the Unique guide
  [IAM (Zitadel) Initial Setup on New Cluster](https://docs.unique.ai/it-operators/identity-and-access-management-iam/iam-zitadel-initial-setup-on-new-cluster):
  project, web application (PKCE), token settings, project roles and the authorization for your user.

  Every request authenticates with `{{pat}}` (a Personal Access Token of a service user with the instance role
  **IAM Owner**, e.g. the `scope-management` service user). Request 01 finds the organization named
  `{{orgName}}` (Cluster IAM) and stores its ID in `orgId`; all later requests act inside it through the
  `x-zitadel-orgid` header.

  Run the requests in order (01 → 07). Requests that create something store the returned IDs
  (`orgId`, `projectId`, `appId`, `clientId`, `userId`) in the active environment for the next requests.

  See README.md in this folder for setup.
}
